{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are implementing GitHub issue #16 (pi backend) in user/delegate. Read `gh issue view 16`, the rulings in `gh issue view 16 --comments`, the amended interface ruling in `gh issue view 15 --comments`, and spec #4 (pi bullet under Backends). Do not delegate further: no subagents, no delegate runs. Follow AGENTS.md. Stay on branch `16-pi` in this worktree; do not create branches. Commit when done (message ends `Co-Authored-By: Muse Spark <noreply@opencode.ai>`); do not push.\n\n## What exists (read first)\n- `src/backends/mod.rs`: `enum Backend { Cursor }` with `from_name`, `name`, `bin`, `argv(model, capability, session, prompt) -> (Vec<String>, bool)`, `spawn(&JobSpec) -> Spawned`, `fill_doctor`, `doctor_lines`.\n- `src/backends/cursor/mod.rs`: `resolve_bin`, `argv`, `spawn` + `drive_streams` (pipes, Activity/Progress/Stderr events, kill by process group), `parse_stdout`, `finish`.\n- `src/backends/types.rs`: `BackendResult { text, session_id, usage, cost_usd, is_error, duration_ms, clean_exit, stderr }` — `cost_usd: Some` overrides the model-table price.\n- Unimplemented backends are rejected generically via `Backend::from_name(..) == None` (src/models.rs:28, src/cli.rs ~605, src/cli_info.rs ~108). Making `from_name(\"pi\")` return `Some` is what enables pi models; claude must stay `None`.\n- Fixtures: `tests/fixtures/pi/*.stdout` (raw `pi -p --mode json` output) with `.argv` beside each.\n\n## Build\n1. New variant `Pi` in the enum (literal: `pub enum Backend { Cursor, Pi }`), `from_name(\"pi\") => Some(Self::Pi)`, `name` \"pi\", and a match arm in every method.\n2. New module `src/backends/pi/mod.rs`:\n   - `resolve_bin`: `PI_BIN` env, then `which pi`, mirroring cursor's.\n   - `argv(model, capability, session, prompt)`: `[\"-p\", \"--mode\", \"json\", \"--model\", <model>, \"--session-id\", <session or a fresh lowercase uuid v4>, \"--\", <prompt>]`, is_write = true. The session id is chosen BEFORE launch; resume passes the same id (pi creates the session if absent, continues it if present). Generate the uuid without a new dependency (the crate already has a `random_uuid`-style helper or libc; search `uuid` in src/ first).\n   - `spawn`: reuse cursor's pipe/kill/drive machinery — move the shared part into `src/backends/mod.rs` or a small shared fn so both backends call it with their own per-line handler and finish; do not copy-paste it.\n   - Parser: one JSON object per line. Ignore unparseable lines. Session id from the `{\"type\":\"session\",\"id\":...}` header. Final text = concatenated `text` parts of the last assistant message in `agent_end.messages` (fall back to the last assistant `message_end`). Usage = sum over assistant `message_end` events of `usage.input`→inputTokens, `usage.output`→outputTokens, `cacheRead`→cacheReadTokens, `cacheWrite`→cacheWriteTokens. Cost = sum of `usage.cost.total` over the same events → `cost_usd: Some(sum)`. `stopReason == \"error\"` → `is_error: Some(true)`, text = `errorMessage`. pi exits 0 on errors: never use the exit code to decide success when an `agent_end` is present. No `agent_end` at all → `is_error: Some(true)`, text \"no result line\" (cancelled runs: the supervisor sets CANCELLED, not you). Progress events: `tool_execution_start` sets last_tool/phase like cursor's tool calls; assistant `message_update` text sets last_assistant.\n   - Literal expected normalized result for `tests/fixtures/pi/plain-answer.stdout`:\n     `BackendResult { text: \"391\\nSTATUS: DONE\", session_id: Some(\"afcd8926-430b-4d9a-a552-d7c6d1b900ba\"), usage: Some(Usage { input_tokens: 5320, output_tokens: 9, cache_read_tokens: 0, cache_write_tokens: 0 }), cost_usd: Some(0.0005365), is_error: None or Some(false), .. }`\n     and for `tool-calls-fix.stdout`: cost_usd ≈ 0.00118532 (5 assistant messages), session `e04e84ae-41c0-4ed8-b9e5-de410d2f3bdf`. Use the real `Usage` field names from src/types.rs.\n3. Read-only: a pi model with `--capability read-only` must make `delegate run` (and `resume`) exit 2 with `pi cannot enforce read-only` on stderr, BEFORE detaching. Find where `run` validates the model/capability up front in src/cli.rs and add the check there (minimal edit).\n4. Doctor: `fill_doctor`/`doctor_lines` arm for pi: binary found + `pi --version`; per configured pi model `pi auth check --model <id>` (missing/failed = warning). Make src/doctor.rs and src/cli_info.rs iterate over every implemented backend that has models in the table instead of hard-coding cursor; claude keeps its skip line.\n5. Tests (all required):\n   - One parser test per `tests/fixtures/pi/*.stdout` (plain-answer, tool-calls-fix, resume-answer, error-bad-model, needs-context, cancelled, and any other pi fixture present) asserting text/session/cost/is_error as applicable.\n   - argv test: fresh run has `--session-id <uuid>`; resume reuses the given id.\n   - e2e in tests/cli_e2e.rs (or a new tests/pi_e2e.rs): a fake `pi` shell script selected by `PI_BIN` that `cat`s `tests/fixtures/pi/plain-answer.stdout`; `delegate run --model opencode-go/muse-spark-1.3-contributor --capability read-write` → `watch` shows DONE with the text and costUsd 0.0005365. Plus `--capability read-only` → exit 2 with the message. Fake agents wait on release files, never sleep, for RUNNING assertions.\n   - Update the unit test that asserts `from_name(\"pi\")` is None.\n6. skills/delegate/SKILL.md: only make pi runnable — the \"Only cursor models run today\" sentence becomes cursor and pi; pi rows in Model picks lose \"(not yet runnable)\"; add one line: pi cannot run read-only (exit 2). Leave claude wording alone (a parallel ticket edits it).\n\n## Fence\nOwns: src/backends/** (new pi module, enum, shared spawn helper), src/doctor.rs, src/cli_info.rs (doctor iteration only), src/models.rs (tests that assert pi is unimplemented), src/cli.rs (read-only check only), tests/** except tests/fixtures/** (read-only), skills/delegate/SKILL.md (lines above only). Forbidden: claude backend code, .github/, scripts/, tests/fixtures/** contents, anything outside this worktree. If you need another file, edit it minimally and list it in your report.\n\n## Done when\n`cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test` all pass (tests/budgets.rs included). Report: commit SHA, test count summary, files touched outside the fence (if any), or a failure triage — nothing in between. Then **Friction**: up to 3 bullets on what slowed you, what this brief got wrong or left out, what you'd change (\"none\" is fine).\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}],"timestamp":1790855479398}}
