{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_01a0f74e10b5736fb0e6bb361d483ad5|fc_01a0f74e10b5736fb0e6bb361d483ad5","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"gh issue view 16; echo ====; gh issue view 16 --comments; echo ====; gh issue view 15 --comments; echo ====; git branch --show-current; git status --short | head -30"},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"title:\tPi backend\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#15, user/delegate#6\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t16\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nPi models run through `delegate`. `pi -p --mode json --model provider/id` with the user's full pi configuration. The session id is chosen before launch with `--session-id`, and resume reuses it. Cost is pi's own reported cost. read-only is rejected for pi models. Doctor checks pi's binary and version, and runs `pi auth check --model` for each pi model.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- # [ ] Parser tests on the recorded pi fixtures: answer, tool calls, resume, error.\n- # [ ] run, resume, cancel and watch work end to end against a fake pi replaying fixtures.\n- # [ ] read-only with a pi model fails with a clear message.\n- # [ ] An opt-in live test does one real round trip and saves a fresh fixture.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #6 Record headless fixtures (recording script and probes)\n- #15 Backend split (prefactor)\n====\n"}],"details":{}}}
{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_01a0f74e10b5736fb0e6bb361d483ad5|fc_01a0f74e10b5736fb0e6bb361d483ad5","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"gh issue view 16; echo ====; gh issue view 16 --comments; echo ====; gh issue view 15 --comments; echo ====; git branch --show-current; git status --short | head -30"},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"title:\tPi backend\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#15, user/delegate#6\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t16\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nPi models run through `delegate`. `pi -p --mode json --model provider/id` with the user's full pi configuration. The session id is chosen before launch with `--session-id`, and resume reuses it. Cost is pi's own reported cost. read-only is rejected for pi models. Doctor checks pi's binary and version, and runs `pi auth check --model` for each pi model.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- # [ ] Parser tests on the recorded pi fixtures: answer, tool calls, resume, error.\n- # [ ] run, resume, cancel and watch work end to end against a fake pi replaying fixtures.\n- # [ ] read-only with a pi model fails with a clear message.\n- # [ ] An opt-in live test does one real round trip and saves a fresh fixture.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #6 Record headless fixtures (recording script and probes)\n- #15 Backend split (prefactor)\n====\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Fake binary:** `PI_BIN` overrides the binary, mirroring `CURSOR_AGENT_BIN`.\n2. **Read-only:** a pi model with `--capability read-only` exits 2 with `pi cannot enforce read-only` on stderr.\n3. **Session:** the run generates a UUID and passes `--session-id`, and resume reuses the same flag and id. pi's first-use stderr warning is not an error.\n4. **Errors:** ERROR comes from `stopReason: \"error\"` with `errorMessage` as the text. The exit code is ignored, because pi exits 0 on errors (#6 probe).\n5. **Cost:** the sum of `usage.cost.total` over assistant `message_end` events. Check the sum against `pi/tool-calls-fix` and note the number in the PR.\n6. **Parser tests:** every `tests/fixtures/pi/*.stdout`, including `needs-context` and `cancelled` (no terminal line, so the supervisor sets CANCELLED).\n7. **Doctor:** wire `pi auth check --model <id>` into the #11 doctor, and delete #11's `backend not implemented` stub for pi.\n--\n====\n"}],"details":{}}}
{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_01a0f74e10b5736fb0e6bb361d483ad5|fc_01a0f74e10b5736fb0e6bb361d483ad5","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"gh issue view 16; echo ====; gh issue view 16 --comments; echo ====; gh issue view 15 --comments; echo ====; git branch --show-current; git status --short | head -30"},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"title:\tPi backend\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tuser (Amogh Akshintala)\nlabels:\tready-for-agent\ncomments:\t1\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\tuser/delegate#15, user/delegate#6\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t16\n--\n## Parent\n\n#4\n\n## What to build\n\nPi models run through `delegate`. `pi -p --mode json --model provider/id` with the user's full pi configuration. The session id is chosen before launch with `--session-id`, and resume reuses it. Cost is pi's own reported cost. read-only is rejected for pi models. Doctor checks pi's binary and version, and runs `pi auth check --model` for each pi model.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- # [ ] Parser tests on the recorded pi fixtures: answer, tool calls, resume, error.\n- # [ ] run, resume, cancel and watch work end to end against a fake pi replaying fixtures.\n- # [ ] read-only with a pi model fails with a clear message.\n- # [ ] An opt-in live test does one real round trip and saves a fresh fixture.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #6 Record headless fixtures (recording script and probes)\n- #15 Backend split (prefactor)\n====\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Fake binary:** `PI_BIN` overrides the binary, mirroring `CURSOR_AGENT_BIN`.\n2. **Read-only:** a pi model with `--capability read-only` exits 2 with `pi cannot enforce read-only` on stderr.\n3. **Session:** the run generates a UUID and passes `--session-id`, and resume reuses the same flag and id. pi's first-use stderr warning is not an error.\n4. **Errors:** ERROR comes from `stopReason: \"error\"` with `errorMessage` as the text. The exit code is ignored, because pi exits 0 on errors (#6 probe).\n5. **Cost:** the sum of `usage.cost.total` over assistant `message_end` events. Check the sum against `pi/tool-calls-fix` and note the number in the PR.\n6. **Parser tests:** every `tests/fixtures/pi/*.stdout`, including `needs-context` and `cancelled` (no terminal line, so the supervisor sets CANCELLED).\n7. **Doctor:** wire `pi auth check --model <id>` into the #11 doctor, and delete #11's `backend not implemented` stub for pi.\n--\n====\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\n## Preflight rulings: orchestrator ruling (owner asleep; reversible)\n\n1. **Interface:** an enum `Backend { Cursor }` (pi and claude variants arrive in #16 and #17), with `match` in each method. No `dyn` trait: three closed variants don't need one. Its methods are `bin`, `argv(model, capability, cwd, session)`, `parse` (stream to a normalized result: text, session id, usage, optional cost, error), `resume_args`, and doctor probes. The CLI `doctor` command stays where #11 put it and calls the probes.\n2. **Encapsulation:** `build_argv`, the capability-to-flag mapping and the cursor binary resolution move into `backends/cursor`. Delete the non-spec capability modes if #13 left any.\n3. **Parsers:** `stream.rs` stays at the crate root, so the #17 Claude parser can reuse it. STATUS-line parsing stays outside the backend, in `output.rs`.\n4. **Fixture tests:** one test for each `tests/fixtures/cursor/*.stdout`. Keep the existing inline tests.\n5. **Failure cases:**\n   - A bad model (empty stdout, exit 1) is an error built from the exit code and stderr.\n   - Lines that don't parse are skipped.\n   - A clean exit with no `result` line is ERROR.\n   - CANCELLED is set by the supervisor, never the parser.\n6. **Behaviour:** unchanged. Existing tests may change their imports only.\n--\nauthor:\tuser\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nAmendment to ruling 1 (orchestrator): the interface as landed in #29 is `from_name`, `name`, `bin`, `argv(model, capability, session, prompt)` (resume flags are built inside `argv`), and `spawn`. #16 and #17 add a `parse` match arm when a second parser exists. `cwd` reaches the child through `JobSpec.cwd`.\n--\n====\n16-pi\n"}],"details":{}}}
