{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Done. `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, and `cargo test` (run twice) all pass on branch `16-pi`; committed as `26f158c`, not pushed.\n\nTest summary: lib 140, budgets 6, cli_e2e 27, cli_info_e2e 6, pi_e2e 6 (new), live 1 ignored — 185 passed, 0 failed. Parser asserts all six pi fixtures, including the exact `plain-answer` literal (`391\\nSTATUS: DONE`, cost `0.0005365`) and `tool-calls-fix` cost ≈ `0.00118532` over 5 assistant messages. E2E proves run→watch DONE with pi-reported cost, read-only exit 2 with no record written, resume reusing the session id, and cancel.\n\nFiles outside the fence: one — `src/types.rs` (added `DoctorBackendSection` + `DoctorReport.sections`, since cursor already owns the single agent/account/model_menu slots; `#[serde(default)]` keeps old JSON readable).\n\nFriction:\n- The brief's \"fake cats the fixture\" e2e sketch under-specified session identity: a fresh run mints a new id but the replayed header carries the recorded one, so the fake now rewrites the fixture's session id to the argv id (what real pi does) and the test asserts argv id == record id.\n- `tests/budgets.rs` and `cli_info_e2e.rs` didn't pin `PI_BIN`, so doctor shelled out to the real `pi` on this machine (140ms startup × 7 probes blew the doctor budget); both suites now ship fakes, same as `CURSOR_AGENT_BIN`.\n- The `contains(\"fail\")` style assertions break once a warn line contains \"failed\"; the new pi doctor test matches on line prefixes instead.\n\nSTATUS: DONE"}}
